  "tldr": "Balanced multiple randomization identifies four marketplace exposure means but reveals only one potential outcome per buyer--seller pair, so the population variance envelope, cross-world covariance, and interaction alignment remain latent. The proposal treats interval construction as a decision problem on the complete observed-table experiment. It derives the aligned Gaussian-chaos boundary, builds globally compatible finite completion games whose primal solutions are observable intervals and whose dual solutions are least-favourable schedule mixtures, and asks for matching risk transfers that identify the exact honest normalized expected-length curve \\(R_\\alpha(\\rho)\\) with certified finite evaluation. The essential advance is the sharp all-policy frontier, not a conservative Wald interval, an oracle spectral calibration, or a generic finite linear program.",
  "project_justification": {
    "gap": "Published MRD theory supplies exact component variances, conservative variance estimators, and Gaussian inference under dominance conditions, but it does not value the best honest interval among all functions of the observed four-block table. Existing completion inversion, expected-measure duality, and slice invariance each omit either global four-schedule compatibility, fixed-half product-slice interactions, or all-rule risk transfer.",
    "niche": "The fixed square-half design isolates an economically relevant decision frontier indexed by the observable-experiment-compatible spectral cap \\(\\rho\\), while retaining latent additive nuisance and unobserved cross-world dependence. This is the smallest benchmark in which persistent interaction chaos and honest adaptation can jointly affect the optimal length constant.",
    "fill": "A single sequence of globally compatible completion games will deliver both sides of the result: an interval computed from the observed table and a dual mixture lower bound against every interval on the same experiment. Alignment-aware replacement, rank truncation, and rational quantization will connect the finite certificates to \\(R_\\alpha(\\rho)\\) with an explicit vanishing error."
  },
  "related_work": "MasoeroEtAl2026MRD is the setup and writing exemplar: it moves from marketplace interference to four exposure means, exact design variances, conservative covariance handling, and Gaussian inference. SudijonoEtAl2026Regression is the closest current MRD limit-theory neighbor; its operator-norm term and rank-one product-normal example motivate retaining aligned chaos rather than imposing normality. EvansHansenStark2005MES supplies the acceptance-function and Bayes--minimax architecture for expected length, while BryanMcMahanSchaferSchneider2007MES supplies finite primal--dual game certificates. RigdonHudgens2015Binary supplies the one-population binary completion feature: each observed outcome leaves one missing binary potential outcome, and exact confidence sets follow from attributable-effect prediction or permutation-test inversion. RigdonHudgens2015Interference supplies a distinct interference feature: under two-stage randomization and stratified interference it bounds compatible four-vector schedules and inverts permutation tests for direct, indirect, total, and overall effects. AronowChangLopatto2025FastExactCI accelerates the former binary count-vector inversion, but that reduction does not preserve a continuous crossed four-schedule experiment. AronowGreenLee2014SharpVariance is the sharp coupling precedent for latent cross-world covariance, not an all-interval MRD result. FilmusKindlerMosselWimmer2018Slice, Section 2.1, defines the swap influence \\(\\operatorname{Inf}^{s}_{ij}(f)=\\mathbb E[(f-f^{(ij)})^2]\\) and its coordinate average; Theorem 5.8 supplies the single-slice low-influence invariance template. NourdinPeccatiReinert2010Universality provides product-space homogeneous-sum replacement ingredients, while Ouimet2022HypergeomLeCam does not cover fixed one-half sampling with schedule-dependent bilinear chaos. BhattacharyaEtAl2024QuadraticChaos informs the canonical non-Gaussian boundary but not its rectangular aligned MRD realizability. DaveziesDHaultfoeuilleGuyonvarch2026TwoWay concerns separately exchangeable sampling and conservative clustered inference rather than fixed-schedule assignment risk. SudijonoDobribanTchetgen2026Minimax optimizes mean-squared error in a one-population binary experiment, not expected confidence-interval length in the observed MRD experiment.",
  "technical_internal_limitation": "A canceled single-row additive schedule can have \\(C=0\\) and can change \\(V^+(Y)\\) by a nonvanishing factor while inducing nearly indistinguishable observed tables. Thus no uniformly relatively consistent plug-in estimator of \\(V^+(Y)\\) is available even at \\(\\rho=0\\). This diagnostic is not a theorem contribution and rules out treating the true envelope or an observed spectral profile as an input to the attaining policy.",
  "honest_scope": "The exact coefficient algebra, candidate slice replacement rate, rank truncation, and finite completion calculations are proof leads rather than established results; every numbered node remains to be proved. The unresolved content is the globally compatible completion quotient and its two-sided all-policy risk transfer. For the additive sanity reduction \\(C=0\\), one has only \\(\\operatorname{Var}_Y(\\widehat\\tau)=\\|a\\|_2^2+\\|b\\|_2^2\\leq V^+(Y)\\) in general. The standard-normal oracle constant \\(2z_{1-\\alpha/2}\\) applies only on the explicitly defined envelope-equality subclass \\(F_n^{=}\\) when \\(M(Y)\\) is supplied; it does not identify the full \\(\\rho=0\\) observed-data frontier.",
  "novelty_justification": "The closest MRD papers optimize or calibrate designated estimators, while the closest minimax confidence-set papers assume explicitly parameterized observation families. The selected kernel instead values every interval policy measurable with respect to the complete four-block MRD observation, retains unobserved scale and cross-world ambiguity through globally fixed schedule completions, and requires one finite primal--dual construction to deliver both observable epsilon-attainment and a lower bound against all rules. The aligned Gaussian-chaos theorem is supporting infrastructure rather than the novelty claim.",
